 ## Architecture Overview
 
-The selected `mindscape` composition runs through one Helix pulse loop:
+The selected `mindscape` composition has an independent receptive inbox, filesystem
+sensor, and motor body alongside the language pulse loop:
 
 ```mermaid
 flowchart TD
-    Input[Messages and observations] --> Pulse[Helix PulseLoop]
-    Pulse --> HelixMemory[mRAG / Context Office / 8D memory]
-    Pulse --> Native[Persistent RWKV / Habitus cortex and graph]
+    Input[Received user messages] --> Inbox[Independent receptive inbox]
+    Sensor[Filesystem sensor: fresh metadata every configured interval] --> Native[Persistent RWKV / Habitus cortex and graph]
+    Inbox --> HelixMemory[mRAG / Context Office / 8D memory]
+    Inbox --> Native
     HelixMemory --> Context[Context Loom: independent memory roles and current work]
     Native --> Context
     Context --> DualRWKV[Dual RWKV-7 Subconscious + Speaker]
-    DualRWKV -->|subconscious motor impulse & natural intention| Authorization[Native SELF ability selection]
+    Context --> Motor[Bootstrap goal policy: integer motor signals and observed target handles]
+    Motor --> Authorization[Native SELF ability selection]
     Authorization --> Body[Workspace action]
     Body --> Return[Actual observation and persisted outcome]
-    Return --> Pulse
+    Return --> Context
     Return --> Native
     DualRWKV -->|message| Direction[Native outward gate and Helix recipient-ID routing]
     Direction --> Channel[Terminal / dashboard / configured communications]
 ```
 
-The bicameral architecture separates the persistent Subconscious (tracking state, memory,
-and motor affordance impulses) from the Speaker (generating natural dialogue, reasoning,
-and intention). Subconscious impulses (`OutputTrunk.DO` / `LOOK`) and natural intentions
-drive workspace actions directly without requiring rigid `<intention>` JSON tool markup.
-Execution requires native SELF authorization and an actual host actuator. A receipt proves
-its particular action outcome, not completion of the whole requested task. The underlying
-Helix application also retains the separate provider/tool and task-cognition routes shown below.
+The body receives explicit user goals, prepares them through production memory and
+Context Loom, and emits numeric motor signals. Foreground speech has no actuator
+authority. The sensor keeps recording changed surroundings during language inference
+and sandbox execution; queued frames subsequently enter the native recurrent state.
+Execution requires native SELF authorization and real sensory returns for each target.
+The initial motor policy is bootstrap scaffolding, not learned autonomous exploration.
+Mindscape also pins auxiliary inference to its declared local provider and disables
+the legacy speech-to-task inception route.
+
+After setup, `venv/bin/python main.py` loads the selected agent's data directory.
+Start the local dashboard with `venv/bin/python dashboard/dashboard.py --port 5050`.
+In Chat, expand **Environment and actions** to see body results independently of
+the language reply. For example:
+
+```text
+Please go to /workshop then open Example.py then run it.
+Please open /bedroom/closet/CaseNotes.txt and /bedroom/closet/SecondNote.txt.
+Please sense .
+```
+
+Paths retain their spelling; quote filenames containing spaces. Running a Python
+file first requires its actual content/hash observation and uses the isolated
+workshop. The goal receptor supports movement, inspection, opening, and execution;
+it reports ambiguous targets rather than inventing filenames or program contents.
+The observation cadence is `mindscape.sensory_interval_seconds` (default one second).
+There are no new generation, action-count, or execution-time ceilings.
 
